s10-10-p4 : Block
s10-10-p4 = prose (cons "The induction principle `safe-ind` constructs an inhabitant from a proof of \(I(g)\) and preservation of \(I\) by every adversarial step. Liveness and convergence require the corresponding assumptions about choices and fairness; those properties are not consequences of safety alone. The network, its states, the adversary and the safety predicate are all definitions of this example. Replicated data types supply a separate established family of convergence and exchange protocols ([59](#ref-59)); the safety theorem here follows from the specific transition relation, not from a generic replication guarantee. A different distributed program may use entirely different mathematics. The general language has not acquired a special `Fleet` primitive by expressing this one." nil)
